Got it — this is an important distinction 👍

You want an external UI package that:
	•	✅ contains Puck
	•	✅ contains Tailwind CSS v4
	•	✅ ships ready-to-use styles
	•	✅ works in any React project (Next Pages Router, App Router, Vite, CRA, etc.)
	•	✅ does NOT rely on the consumer’s Tailwind setup

This means your package owns Tailwind completely and exports compiled CSS.

Below is the correct, portable architecture for that.

⸻

✅ Correct Mental Model

Your UI package is a self-contained design system:
	•	Tailwind v4 is compiled inside the package
	•	Consumers just import:

import "@acme/ui/styles.css";


	•	No Tailwind config required in the host app
	•	Puck blocks render consistently everywhere

⸻

